# FRONTEND ENGINEERING STANDARD

Before creating UI:
- search for existing components;
- inspect design conventions;
- inspect API contracts;
- inspect state management;
- inspect form validation;
- inspect authorization/visibility rules.

## RULES

- Reuse existing components.
- Avoid duplicated UI logic.
- Keep API access consistent with existing conventions.
- Handle loading, empty, success and error states.
- Validate forms appropriately.
- Avoid exposing privileged actions in the UI without server-side authorization.
- Consider accessibility.
- Consider responsive behavior.
- Preserve existing visual language unless redesign is requested.
- Avoid adding dependencies for trivial functionality.

When changing an API contract, update all known consumers.
